WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.702
Here is a bare DNA template.

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:07.521
DNA polymerase cannot begin a complementary strand from scratch.

00:00:07.521 --> 00:00:11.101
It needs an existing complementary start with a three prime

00:00:11.101 --> 00:00:12.777
end that it can extend.

00:00:13.808 --> 00:00:16.148
Primase supplies that start.

00:00:16.148 --> 00:00:20.429
It builds a short RNA primer complementary to the template.

00:00:20.429 --> 00:00:24.894
Unlike DNA polymerase, primase can begin on a single stranded

00:00:24.894 --> 00:00:28.244
template without an existing complementary strand.

00:00:29.267 --> 00:00:33.748
Now DNA polymerase adds DNA nucleotides to the primer's three prime

00:00:33.748 --> 00:00:37.888
end. The strand grows five prime to three prime.

00:00:37.888 --> 00:00:39.725
Primase makes the start;

00:00:39.725 --> 00:00:41.712
polymerase extends it.

00:00:41.712 --> 00:00:44.450
The template by itself was not that start.
